    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks very much for helping me here. Can we conclude that there is only a nonconstructive bijection and \"function to function relation\" (aesop works for the last sorry within it)?</p>\n<p>I would like to add for clarity that when I accomplished the goal, <code>get_value_from_relation</code> was prefixed with <code>nonconstructive</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mathlibStandardSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">relation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ord</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">function_relation</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\